// Title: Potential Renamed Rundll32 Execution
// Sigma ID: 2569ed8c-1147-498a-9b8c-2ad3656b10ed
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-08-22 | Modified: 2023-02-03
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects when 'DllRegisterServer' is called in the commandline and the image is not rundll32.
//   This could mean that the 'rundll32' utility has been renamed in order to avoid detection
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/swisscom_csirt/status/1331634525722521602?s=20
//   - https://app.any.run/tasks/f74c5157-8508-4ac6-9805-d63fe7b0d399/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_rundll32_dllregisterserver.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "DllRegisterServer" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe"))
